  "summary": "This study compares pristine Ti3C2Tx MXene hydrogel (MH) with holey-MXene hydrogels etched for 1, 3, or 6 h (HMH1, HMH3, and HMH6). Ti3C2Tx was prepared by LiF/HCl MILD etching, assembled using [Zn(NH3)4]2+ cations, acid-washed, then oxidatively acid-etched in 3 M H2SO4 at 60 \u00b0C. HMH3 was the headline electrode, reaching 359.2 F g\u22121 at 10 mV s\u22121; at 10.1 mg cm\u22122 it achieved 3.84 F cm\u22122 at 10 mV s\u22121. A separately fabricated vacuum-filtered HMH3 film delivered 1606.8 F cm\u22123 at 10 mV s\u22121. Mass loading is absent for the standard gravimetric tests, and no numerical tortuosity or lateral flake sizes are reported."
}